* Each request has a TYPE (HTTP Method).
  - EX: axios.get('api/cart-items');

    - Sends 2 pieces of information: type and URL path
      -  GET and 'api/cart-items'

    - EX: axios.post('api/cart-items');

    - Sends 2 pieces of information: type and URL path
      -  POST and 'api/cart-items'

* When backend receives our request, it looks at BOTH the type and URL path to decide what to do.

* 4 common types of requests:
  - GET = get some data

  - POST = create some data

  - PUT = update some data

  - DELETE = delete some data

* Axios has a method for each type:
  - axios.get('api/cart-items');

  - axios.post('api/cart-items');

  - axios.put('api/cart-items');

  - axios.delete('api/cart-items');

